ffmpeg-rockchip (8.0.3-1+rkmpp.20260423.6404384) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Built from nyanmisaka/ffmpeg-rockchip 64043842f83b49a729f0c677fce7196f3eff49e4,
    the 8.0 branch. 8.0.3 is the RELEASE file at that commit; +rkmpp is the
    baseline, the fork's six commits on top of upstream ffmpeg that add the
    MPP hwcontext, the decoders, the encoders, the RGA filters and NV15/NV20.
  * The tree carries no debian/, so all of it is ours.
  * libav* are linked in statically, so this package ships no shared library
    and cannot shadow the distro's libavcodec.so.62. That matters: 135
    packages in the Ubuntu archive link against it, 12 of them installed on a
    desktop image, and replacing it would put us on the hook for matching
    Ubuntu's whole feature set and for its ffmpeg CVE rebases.

 -- Mixtile <dev@mixtile.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 07:00:00 +0000
